# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Without this file, Git falls back to each developer's `core.autocrlf` setting,
# which on Windows rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. Prettier is configured
# with `endOfLine: "lf"`, so those checkouts report a `Delete ␍` error on every
# line of every file. Settings here are committed, so they apply to everyone and
# to CI; `core.autocrlf` is per-machine and cannot be relied on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, so Git never inspects or rewrites their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
